--TEST--
A derived decoder reports four bad fields in one `ParseError`, each at its own dotted path, and the constructor does not run — `rule:core-classes/derive-reports-every-field`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Every field of `Order` is wrong in a different way: a wrong type, a missing
// key, a bad list element and a bad field of a nested class.
#[Core\Json\Derive]
class Address {
    public function constructor(public string $city) {}
}

#[Core\Json\Derive]
class Order {
    public function constructor(
        public int $id,
        public string $name,
        public array<int> $tags,
        public Address $address,
    ) {
        echo "constructor ran\n";
    }
}

try {
    Core\Json::decodeAs<Order>("{\"id\":\"seven\",\"tags\":[1,\"two\"],\"address\":{\"city\":5}}");
    echo "not reached\n";
} catch (ParseError $bad) {
    echo "issues=", Core\Arr::count($bad->issues) as string, "\n";
    foreach ($bad->issues as var $issue) {
        echo $issue->path, ": ", $issue->message, "\n";
    }
}
--EXPECT--
issues=4
id: expected int, found a string
name: required field missing
tags.1: expected int, found a string
address.city: expected string, found a number
